<body>
<div style="--ark-accent: #b8480f; --ark-accent-hover: #8f3709; --ark-border: #e8dccb; background: #faf6f0; margin: -2.5rem -1.5rem -4rem; padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 4rem"><header class="cluster"><nav class="nav"><a href="index.html">Home</a><a href="bundle-size.html">Bundle Size</a><a href="adoption.html">Adoption</a><a href="architecture.html">Architecture</a><a href="methodology.html">Methodology</a><a href="verdict.html">Verdict</a><a href="getting-started.html">Getting Started</a><a href="changelog.html">Changelog</a><a href="faq.html">FAQ</a><a href="playground.html">Playground</a></nav></header><main class="page"><div class="hero"><h1>ARKlight vs. Traditional Frontend Frameworks</h1><p>Python compiles to static HTML on one side. Runtime JavaScript frameworks -- React, Vue, Svelte, Angular -- on the other. This site compares them on real, sourced numbers, including bundle sizes ARKlight measured on itself, not just quoted from an article.</p></div><h2>At a glance</h2><div class="switcher"><div class="card"><h3 class="kpi-value">0.5 KB</h3><p class="muted">ARKlight, static page, zero shipped JS beyond nav-highlighting</p><meter value="0.5" min="0" max="50">ARKlight static</meter></div><div class="card"><h3 class="kpi-value">5.98 KB</h3><p class="muted">ARKlight, a page using State/Bind/Action</p><meter value="5.98" min="0" max="50">ARKlight stateful</meter></div><div class="card"><h3 class="kpi-value">42-48 KB</h3><p class="muted">React + ReactDOM baseline, before app code</p><meter value="45" min="0" max="50">React baseline</meter></div></div><h2>Where to go from here</h2><div class="grid"><a href="bundle-size.html" class="card">Bundle Size &amp; Performance</a><a href="adoption.html" class="card">Market Share &amp; Developer Sentiment</a><a href="architecture.html" class="card">How Each Tool Actually Works</a><a href="playground.html" class="card">Try It -- Live State/Bind/Action Demo</a><a href="methodology.html" class="card">Methodology &amp; Sources</a><a href="verdict.html" class="card bento-hero">The Honest Verdict -- who should (and shouldn&#x27;t) use ARKlight</a></div></main><footer><p class="muted">ARKlight vs. Traditional Frontend Frameworks -- a comparison site built in ARKlight, about ARKlight.</p><a href="arklight-vs-frontend.ark" class="source-note">Download offline bundle (.ark)</a></footer></div>
<script>
